 "content_notes": "Tone: absurd; the joke is on the schemes, never on the victims (the bridge's owner, the resort developer and the national park are never shown or mocked). The two Pennsylvania brothers (October 2011) were CHARGED only and no plea, verdict or sentence was found in any report: never named, drawn ONLY as dark rim-lit silhouettes tagged NOT A LIKENESS, every claim attributed ('police say', BOTH CHARGED, AS OF OCT 2026); the headline 'THEY STOLE AN ENTIRE BRIDGE' names nobody. The sand loader is an anonymous generic silhouette (nobody was named in any report; no arrest or outcome is claimed). The Chilean driver (February 2012) is ACCUSED only: never named, silhouette, 'police say'; no court outcome found. The scrapyard worker and the two officers are generic figures; no force beyond hands behind the back, no weapon shown or mentioned. The phone screen shows only our own drawn bridge thumbnail (no app or interface imitated); the scrapyard sign, the resort sign and the police vehicles carry plain type and no company, force or brand marking. The creek, the scrapyard, both beaches, the road and the truck are illustrations, not reported scenes. Every card is our own typed graphic. No dialogue or quotation card. Facts verified 2026-10-20.",
